{"title":"Career Roadmap · Optical Store Manager","role":"Optical Store Manager","summary":"An Optical Store Manager combines optometry knowledge with retail operations, customer service, inventory management, optical product knowledge, sales, staff supervision, and business management.","facts":{"Current degree":"Allied Health Sciences (B.Sc / BPT / BOT / BMLT etc.)","Course":"Optometry (B.Optom)"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"An Optical Store Manager combines optometry knowledge with retail operations, customer service, inventory management, optical product knowledge, sales, staff supervision, and business management."},{"type":"p","text":"A B.Optom graduate has an advantage over a general retail manager because they can understand vision needs, spectacle prescriptions, lenses, frames, contact lenses, optical measurements, and patient/customer requirements while managing the commercial side of an optical business."},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest career positioning is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Optometry","Optical Dispensing","Retail Operations","Sales","Inventory","Customer Experience","Business Analytics"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"flow","items":["Store Manager","Cluster/Area Manager","Optical Operations Manager","Regional Head","Optical Business Manager/Entrepreneur"],"label":"The role can develop into"}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Development Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"B.Optom, clinical optometry, dispensing, lens/frame knowledge and customer communication"}],[{"text":"2030–2033"},{"text":"Optometrist / Optical Consultant → develop retail and store-management skills"}],[{"text":"2033–2038"},{"text":"Senior Optometrist / Assistant Store Manager → operations, inventory and team management"}],[{"text":"2038–2044"},{"text":"Optical Store Manager → mult