endor management"},{"text":"Basic exposure"}],[{"text":"Business fundamentals"},{"text":"Intermediate"}],[{"text":"Clinical internship"},{"text":"Strong"}],[{"text":"Retail internship"},{"text":"Strong"}],[{"text":"Portfolio"},{"text":"4–6 business/clinical projects"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Best Overall Positioning"},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest pathway is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Optom","Optometrist/Optical Consultant","Retail Optical Experience","Senior Optometrist/Assistant Store Manager","Optical Store Manager","Cluster/Area Manager"]},{"type":"p","text":"For a future-ready Optical Store Manager, the ideal combination is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Optometry","optical dispensing","customer experience","retail sales","inventory management","staff leadership","business analytics","digital/AI-enabled optical retail."],"sep":"+"},{"type":"note","label":"Database note","text":"“Optical Store Manager” is a strong and realistic career target for B.Optom, but it is generally a post-experience management role rather than a direct fresh-graduate position. The roadmap should therefore show Optometrist/Optical Consultant → Assistant Store Manager → Store Manager as the primary progression."}]}]}